            <ArticleTitle>Unstable Angina Pectoris in a 22-year-old Female Patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>33-37</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2739/kurumemedj.MS6300008</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Because of the protective effect of estrogen for atherosclerosis, the prevalence of acute coronary syndrome in women before menopause is low. We report a rare case of unstable angina in a young Japanese female who had a history of cigarette smoking and contraceptive use. Her coronary stenosis was successfully treated by percutaneous coronary intervention.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
